Ever since I beagn playing board games, I've always solo. That was my number one criteria in a game. Never occured to me who was the designer the game. I just played games because of the interesting mechanics or theme.

## Discovering David Turzi

It all began with Anachrony. I stumbled upon someone selling the game on Facebook Marketplace and noticed numerous comments about it on BoardGameGeek. I watched several videos and eventually added it to my wishlist. Then, one day, while browsing a local board game store, I saw Anachrony prominently displayed on the shelf.

I took it out and was struck by its beauty—a solid, heavy box. At that point, I still didn’t care much of the designer. I immediately pulled out my phone and messaged the seller on Facebook Marketplace. He was also offering the expansion "Fractures of Time," which I needed for its solo mode.

A few days later, I received the game and explored its various solo modes. I was amazed by how well it played solo, almost as if it were designed for human interaction. Compared to other solo games I’ve played, such as Lost Ruins of Arnak, Endless Winter, and Tapestry, this one ranked exceptionally high for me in terms of solo play.

Then eventually Voidfall began buzzing around being published by Mindclash. No clue who Mindclash was and again never bothered who the designer. I finally searched them up. My jaw stayed open for few seconds. David Turzi name was mentioned from the creator of Anachrony. Really? I pulled out box of Anachrony and I see his name. At the same time I was highly interested in Nucluem and AGAIN David's name appearing. I was thinking, why am I drawn so much to this particular designer?

David Turci is one of my favorite board game designers because his games are known for their innovative mechanics, engaging themes, and strategic depth. His ability to create immersive experiences that challenge players while providing replayability is truly impressive. Whether it's through unique gameplay mechanics or well-crafted narratives, Turci consistently delivers memorable and enjoyable gaming experiences.
